  "slug": "photonic-edge-025e",
  "summary": "Recent preprints report exact mobility edges, coupling-sign control of flatband formation, and antihelical edge states in photonic platforms.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the engineering of localized and confined optical modes in photonic platforms, with flat bands and bound states in the continuum as the dominant theme. Three of the four preprints address this directly. In C2-symmetric photonic-crystal slabs, a four-mode non-Hermitian model shows that coupling sign controls BIC merging and flatband formation, with Q scaling as k^-6. In one-dimensional non-Hermitian pseudospin lattices, non-Hermiticity is shown to embed compact localized states within a continuum. An experimental preprint realizes exact mobility edges and flat-band states in a two-dimensional photonic quasicrystal using auxiliary subsystems and photonic waveguides. The fourth item, a proposal for antihelical gapless edge states in a photonic metacrystal with staggered bianisotropy, addresses edge states rather than flat bands. What is new is explicit tuning of flatband and BIC physics through coupling sign and non-Hermiticity, together with experimental verification of exact mobility edges.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
